  "summary": "The figure presents Arrhenius plots of ln(\u03c3T) versus 1000/T for five different compositions, indicated by 'x' values ranging from 0 to 0.30. All compositions exhibit a linear decrease in ln(\u03c3T) with increasing 1000/T, which corresponds to decreasing temperature, signifying activated conduction. A general trend observed is that as the 'x' value increases, the overall conductivity (represented by ln(\u03c3T)) decreases across the entire measured temperature range. Furthermore, the slope of the lines becomes slightly steeper with increasing 'x', suggesting a moderate increase in the activation energy for conduction as the 'x' composition increases."
